"and track costs. Other MCP servers are dumb pipes."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:154
msgid "Embedded LLM Gateway"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:155
msgid ""
"Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Bedrock, Azure OpenAI, Ollama, OpenAI-compatible endpoints and more, "
"from one provider registry that custom providers join. DB-managed models with user-level "
"overrides."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/ai/ai_settings.html:227 sajha/web/templates/landing.html:157
msgid "Semantic Tool Discovery"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:158
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Describe what you need in English. Vector embeddings of %(tool_count)s tool descriptions resolve "
"intent to the right tool with confidence scores and auto-extracted parameters."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/composite/builder.html:25 sajha/web/templates/landing.html:160
msgid "Composite Tools"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:161
msgid ""
"Chain multiple tools into one call. Sibling pattern runs tools in parallel. Parent-Child fans out"
" per record. Dynamic schemas built at boot from DB definitions."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:163
msgid "OpenTelemetry Observability"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:164
msgid ""
"Per-tool p50/p95/p99 latency histograms. Error spike alerting. Health probes for Kubernetes. "
"Optional OTEL SDK exports to Datadog, Grafana, Splunk."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:166
msgid "Governed Access"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:167
msgid ""
"Roles with wildcard tool permissions, per-API-key allowlists and denylists, and policy rules that"
" deny, require approval, constrain arguments or meter quotas on every tool call."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:169
msgid "Plugin System"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:170
msgid ""
"Drop a plugin directory with JSON tool configs or Python classes. Auto-discovered, checksum-"
"verified, dependency-installed. Publish and share tool packs."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:172
msgid "Multi-Layer Security"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:173
msgid ""
"SAJHA JWTs, API keys and the session cookie, plus OAuth 2.1 on <code>/mcp</code> from the built-"
"in authorization server or an external issuer. RBAC with wildcard tool permissions. Every call "
"authenticated, authorised, and audit-logged."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:176
msgid ""
"7 visual tool creators: Python, REST, DB Query, Script, PowerBI Report, PowerBI DAX, LiveLink. "
"Analysts create tools without writing code. Hot-reload deploys in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:178
msgid "Tool Versioning"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:179
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Run v1 and v2 side-by-side. Deprecation lifecycle with sunset dates. Contract testing validates "
"all %(tool_count)s tools against live APIs. Zero surprises in production."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:185
msgid "Connectivity"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:186
msgid "Streamable HTTP for every client. Legacy transports for the rest."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:187
msgid ""
"Every transport reaches the same MCPHandler: identical JSON-RPC 2.0, same auth, same audit "
"logging."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:192
msgid ""
"Both eras: stateless 2026-07-28 requests and 2025-11-25 sessions. What every current MCP client "
"uses."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:195
msgid "HTTP+SSE (legacy)"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:196
msgid ""
"The 2024-11-05 transport, with <code>POST /mcp/message</code>, for older clients that predate "
"Streamable HTTP."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:199
msgid "WebSocket (extension)"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:200
msgid ""
"A SAJHA extension: full-duplex, with change notifications pushed. Authenticates with a SAJHA JWT "
"or API key."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:207
msgid "The wire, live"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/landing.html:208
msgid ""
"What a 2026-07-28 client and SAJHA actually say to each other: no handshake, no session, every "
"request complete in itself."
msgstr ""

