#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:23
msgid "What SAJHA is"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:25
msgid ""
"SAJHA turns a catalog of data and utility tools (market data, central banks, public statistics, "
"filings, search, analytics, calculators) and reusable prompts into something any MCP client can "
"discover and call: an AI assistant, an agent framework or a script."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:26
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Around that core it adds what running such a server needs: a web console, users and roles, API "
"keys, OAuth 2.1 on <code>/mcp</code>, a sandbox for user code, a visual tool builder, tool "
"composition, proxied MCP servers, SAJHA Net for sharing tools between servers, an intelligence "
"layer that answers questions with the tools, LLM tools, workflows, policies and a tamper-evident "
"audit, caching, circuit breakers, observability, shared state for several workers and pluggable "
"storage. <a href=\"%(value)s\">How SAJHA fits together</a> · <a href=\"%(value2)s\">How it "
"compares</a>."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:39
msgid "The name"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:44
msgid ""
"<strong>SAJHA</strong> (Hindi: साझा, Urdu: ساجھا) means <em>shared</em>, <em>common</em> or "
"<em>collaborative</em>: one server whose tools many clients share."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:51
msgid "Running now"
msgstr ""

