msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:72
msgid "One <code>/mcp</code> endpoint serves both eras, chosen per request:"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:74
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>Stateless</strong> (%(modern_versions)s): no handshake and no session; every request is "
"complete in itself."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:75
#, python-format
msgid ""
"<strong>Session-based</strong> (%(handshake_versions)s): <code>initialize</code> first, then "
"requests on the session."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:77
#, python-format
msgid ""
"How it works: the <a href=\"%(value)s\">MCP Protocol Guide</a>. What was tested, with the "
"conformance-suite results and known limits: <a href=\"%(value2)s\">2026-07-28</a> and <a "
"href=\"%(value3)s\">2025-11-25</a> compliance reports."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:86
msgid "Access"
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:89
msgid ""
"SAJHA's own credentials: a login session, a SAJHA JWT, or an API key limited to the tools it may "
"call. Roles decide what each account can do in the console."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:90
msgid ""
"OAuth 2.1 on <code>/mcp</code>, set by <code>mcp.auth.mode</code>: <code>off</code> (the "
"default), <code>optional</code> or <code>required</code>; tokens from the built-in authorization "
"server or an external issuer."
msgstr ""

#: sajha/web/templates/help/about.html:91
msgid ""
"Console single sign-on with an organisation's OpenID Connect identity provider "
"(<code>auth.sso</code>, off by default), alongside passwords and API keys. OAuth on "
"<code>/mcp</code> is separate from it, and SAJHA is not an OpenID Connect provider."
msgstr ""

